    "agent_last_message": "I've written the tool as a single file, `output/main.py`, using only the standard library. I ran three quick checks and all gave the expected result:\n- **Normal file:** a small sample with mixed case, punctuation, a blank line and no trailing newline produced the expected counts, and `top_words` was in the right order.\n- **Missing input file:** exits with code 1.\n- **Bad arguments:** exits with code 1.\n\nI didn't test the empty file, a whitespace-only file or very large files.\n\nHow it follows the spec:\n- **Characters** are bytes in the file.\n- **Lines** are the number of `\\n` characters, plus one if the file doesn't end with a newline. An empty file has 0 lines.\n- **Words** are split only on the six whitespace characters the spec lists (space, tab, newline, carriage return, form feed, vertical tab). They're lowercased for counting, so `hello,` and `hello` stay separate words.\n- **`top_words`** is the 10 most frequent words, sorted by count (highest first) and then alphabetically.\n\nThree choices the spec didn't settle:\n- **Text encoding:** I treat the input as UTF-8. A file that isn't valid UTF-8 counts as \"malformed\" and exits with code 1. If your files include other encodings such as Latin-1, this will reject them.\n- **Output file can't be written:** this also exits with code 1.\n- **Any other unexpected error:** exits with code 2.\n\nRun it as `python main.py --input <file> --output <result.json>`.",
